1
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:09,800
Hey!

2
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:11,700
All clear!

3
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:12,900
Take a look!

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,100
A mobile phone!

5
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:17,800
You think they bought Tom Thomas a new one?

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,300
Oh, wow!

7
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:21,300
Nolik, stop!

8
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:23,000
Awesome!

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,500
Turn around!

10
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:34,480
Tom Thomas, help us, please!

11
00:00:34,679 --> 00:00:36,880
We're trying to save your telephone!

12
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,439
That's not mine!

13
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:41,000
Oh! Katya left it behind!

14
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:43,039
Katya!

15
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:44,920
Katya!

16
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,159
She's gone. It's too late.

17
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:51,640
Oh, an SMS just came in.

18
00:00:51,719 --> 00:00:53,160
You won't read it, will you?

19
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:54,760
Of course not.

20
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:57,280
But what if it's something important?

21
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:01,200
Tom Thomas, don't you even dare go and read her letters!

22
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:03,359
Uh-huh, pretty interesting.

23
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:06,280
Lookie, there's just a ton of these messages!

24
00:01:06,439 --> 00:01:09,719
Now, Nolik, you go and distract him from the telephone.

25
00:01:09,799 --> 00:01:10,560
Uh-huh!

26
00:01:19,319 --> 00:01:20,960
Chewsocka, hey!

27
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:23,280
It's me, your buddy Nolik!

28
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,800
Hey there!

29
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:39,800
Cut it out!

30
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Stop it! That's enough with the barking! Out of this room! Right now!

31
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Done! Well, power's off now.

32
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:13,000
Huh? What's up? It stopped working all of a sudden!

33
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:15,200
Oh, it looks like you've broken it!

34
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:16,400
What? No way!

35
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:17,500
You did too!

36
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,200
Well, Tom Thomas,

37
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:21,800
now you'll have to give Katya your phone back like this.

38
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:24,500
I just don't get it.

39
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:29,159
It happened because you were reading someone else's mail.

40
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:30,719
It was just an SMS.

41
00:02:33,819 --> 00:02:36,719
An SMS is no different from a letter.

42
00:02:36,979 --> 00:02:37,979
It's only shorter.

43
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:41,039
People send SMSs through their mobile phones.

44
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:45,180
And that's why looking inside someone else's phone and reading their SMSs

45
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:47,520
is just as rude as reading someone else's mail.

46
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:51,180
And that's why when we Fixies work inside of a phone,

47
00:02:51,479 --> 00:02:54,379
we always put our headphones on when a call comes in

48
00:02:54,379 --> 00:02:58,579
so we won't overhear people's private conversations by accident.

49
00:02:59,019 --> 00:03:01,259
It's just the polite thing to do.

50
00:03:04,019 --> 00:03:06,979
I promise I won't read anyone else's messages.

51
00:03:07,219 --> 00:03:09,579
But that's not going to make the mobile work again.

52
00:03:09,699 --> 00:03:11,740
Now what? Tell them the truth?

53
00:03:13,419 --> 00:03:17,500
Don't you worry, Tom Thomas, because we turned the phone off.

54
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:19,340
And now we'll turn it back on.

55
00:03:25,379 --> 00:03:28,379
See that? The contact's barely attached.

56
00:03:29,379 --> 00:03:32,859
We just need to write a note to the Fixies who work over at Katya's.

57
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:34,500
I'm sure they'll fix it.

58
00:03:37,379 --> 00:03:41,780
There are Fixies living in every home, and the work they have to do can seem endless.

59
00:03:41,939 --> 00:03:45,180
The TV starts acting up, then the doorbell breaks,

60
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:48,979
the washing machine stops running, and then the phone won't ring.

61
00:03:49,099 --> 00:03:52,500
And besides all of that, there is cleaning and there's oiling.

62
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:56,939
Like the appliances in the kitchen or kids' toys and all those other things,

63
00:03:56,939 --> 00:04:00,780
modern houses are literally stuffed with all sorts of devices.

64
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:05,139
And that is why the Fixies keep working day in and day out.

65
00:04:05,139 --> 00:04:09,460
Unfortunately, this can make Fixies get carried away by their jobs.

66
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:12,699
And they can forget about their Fixie relatives and close friends

67
00:04:12,699 --> 00:04:15,340
that live in the neighboring houses and apartments.

68
00:04:15,340 --> 00:04:16,939
That's not right!

69
00:04:16,939 --> 00:04:21,459
Just like humans, Fixies have to remember to go and visit each other more often

70
00:04:21,459 --> 00:04:25,019
and write each other letters, or at least send their regards.

71
00:04:29,579 --> 00:04:31,659
That's all! It's working again!

72
00:04:31,979 --> 00:04:32,979
You're the best!

73
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:36,539
Now I can give a call to Katya and tell her she left her phone over here.

74
00:04:40,539 --> 00:04:43,500
Talk to Elvis! Is that you calling?

75
00:04:43,740 --> 00:04:44,579
Yeah.

76
00:04:44,779 --> 00:04:46,219
And to who?

77
00:04:46,419 --> 00:04:47,419
Katya.

78
00:04:48,179 --> 00:04:49,819
And her phone is where?

79
00:04:51,459 --> 00:04:57,500
Ha-ha-ha!

80
00:04:57,900 --> 00:04:59,900
Tom Thomas, good catch!

81
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Boy, you're fast, just like, uh, like, uh, like a Fixie!

